            "body": "Thanks  a lot! Yes, it did :-)\r\n\r\nAfter some more investigation this seems to be a UI glitch in my environment. E.g. after applying a hunk (via `gh`) the UI isn't updated:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f0289c02-806c-4074-91b2-f05cfd64a3c7)\r\n\r\nI first need to reload the file with `:e` to see the applied hunk:\r\n ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/028df6ea-e6e2-444f-983d-c35c397ad27a)\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks  a lot! Yes, it did :-)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">After some more investigation this seems to be a UI glitch in my environment. E.g. after applying a hunk (via <code class=\"notranslate\">gh</code>) the UI isn't updated:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/18331923/385194801-f0289c02-806c-4074-91b2-f05cfd64a3c7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..K0jEb69nYgUHnD4wrMzEWi2EMFuuKEgxZQZQYwwH_oM\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/18331923/385194801-f0289c02-806c-4074-91b2-f05cfd64a3c7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..K0jEb69nYgUHnD4wrMzEWi2EMFuuKEgxZQZQYwwH_oM\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I first need to reload the file with <code class=\"notranslate\">:e</code> to see the applied hunk:<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/18331923/385199957-028df6ea-e6e2-444f-983d-c35c397ad27a.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..FBCNHx4npM3EynNjrPRMPNgpJBVUw-YsX7NLMgDj2CY\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/18331923/385199957-028df6ea-e6e2-444f-983d-c35c397ad27a.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..FBCNHx4npM3EynNjrPRMPNgpJBVUw-YsX7NLMgDj2CY\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>",
            "bodyText": "Thanks  a lot! Yes, it did :-)\nAfter some more investigation this seems to be a UI glitch in my environment. E.g. after applying a hunk (via gh) the UI isn't updated:\n\nI first need to reload the file with :e to see the applied hunk:",
