                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> After some more investigation this seems to be a UI glitch in my environment. E.g. after applying a hunk (via `gh`) the UI isn't updated:\r\n\r\nThis should not happen. Here is how it works for me locally (with 'signcolumn=auto'):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7512cd49-e330-413c-9589-332c0a2c1afa\r\n\r\nWhat Neovim version and OS are you using? And just to be sure, did you disable 'gitsigns.nvim' (so that it doesn't run in parallel with 'mini.diff')?",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">After some more investigation this seems to be a UI glitch in my environment. E.g. after applying a hunk (via <code class=\"notranslate\">gh</code>) the UI isn't updated:</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This should not happen. Here is how it works for me locally (with 'signcolumn=auto'):</p>\n<details open=\"\" class=\"details-reset border rounded-2\">\n  <summary class=\"tmp-px-3 py-2\">\n    <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" data-component=\"Octicon\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-device-camera-video\">\n    <path d=\"M16 3.75v8.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.136.643L11 10.575v.675A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 13h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25v-6.5C0 3.784.784 3 1.75 3h7.5c.966 0 1.75.784 1.75 1.75v.675l3.864-2.318A.75.75 0 0 1 16 3.75Zm-6.5 1a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25h-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v6.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-6.5ZM11 8.825l3.5 2.1v-5.85l-3.5 2.1Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n    <span class=\"m-1\">minidiff_add-with-signcolumn.mp4</span>\n    <span class=\"dropdown-caret\"></span>\n  </summary>\n\n  <video src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/24854248/385234000-7512cd49-e330-413c-9589-332c0a2c1afa.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..01mK3xsOshPsb9t732qhGqDWiE2McLy9VybYChAaaNA\" data-canonical-src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/24854248/385234000-7512cd49-e330-413c-9589-332c0a2c1afa.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..01mK3xsOshPsb9t732qhGqDWiE2McLy9VybYChAaaNA\" controls=\"controls\" muted=\"muted\" class=\"d-block rounded-bottom-2 border-top width-fit\" style=\"max-height:640px; min-height: 200px\">\n\n  </video>\n</details>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">What Neovim version and OS are you using? And just to be sure, did you disable 'gitsigns.nvim' (so that it doesn't run in parallel with 'mini.diff')?</p>",
                    "bodyText": "After some more investigation this seems to be a UI glitch in my environment. E.g. after applying a hunk (via gh) the UI isn't updated:\n\nThis should not happen. Here is how it works for me locally (with 'signcolumn=auto'):\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    minidiff_add-with-signcolumn.mp4\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n\nWhat Neovim version and OS are you using? And just to be sure, did you disable 'gitsigns.nvim' (so that it doesn't run in parallel with 'mini.diff')?",
