            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "Thx, I really appreciate you taking the time to look at this.\r\n\r\n- yes, I disabled gitsigns.nvim\r\n- signcolumn=auto, too\r\n- Neovim version:  v0.10.1 (LuaJIT 2.1.1713484068)\r\n- OS: OpenBSD 7.6, amd64\r\n\r\nTo be honest, Gitsigns has the same problem (not updating the UI after applying a hunk). The problem there is luv:\r\nhttps://github.com/lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim/blob/main/lua/gitsigns/watcher.lua#L146-L152\r\n\r\nMaybe this is OpenBSD related. I don't want to bother you with stuff you're not using....",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thx, I really appreciate you taking the time to look at this.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>yes, I disabled gitsigns.nvim</li>\n<li>signcolumn=auto, too</li>\n<li>Neovim version:  v0.10.1 (LuaJIT 2.1.1713484068)</li>\n<li>OS: OpenBSD 7.6, amd64</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To be honest, Gitsigns has the same problem (not updating the UI after applying a hunk). The problem there is luv:<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim/blob/main/lua/gitsigns/watcher.lua#L146-L152\">https://github.com/lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim/blob/main/lua/gitsigns/watcher.lua#L146-L152</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Maybe this is OpenBSD related. I don't want to bother you with stuff you're not using....</p>",
            "bodyText": "Thx, I really appreciate you taking the time to look at this.\n\nyes, I disabled gitsigns.nvim\nsigncolumn=auto, too\nNeovim version:  v0.10.1 (LuaJIT 2.1.1713484068)\nOS: OpenBSD 7.6, amd64\n\nTo be honest, Gitsigns has the same problem (not updating the UI after applying a hunk). The problem there is luv:\nhttps://github.com/lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim/blob/main/lua/gitsigns/watcher.lua#L146-L152\nMaybe this is OpenBSD related. I don't want to bother you with stuff you're not using....",
